- Story & Context: Decades after the engines went silent and the generation ship entered the dim crimson gravitational wake of Proxima Centauri b, salvage drones found Deck Zero encrusted in crystallized sweat, engine soot, and the broken remnants of eighty wooden bachi sticks. The great oak Nagado-daiko remained mounted to the bow frame, its drumhead stained with oxidized rust and carved with the funeral dates of three generations who drummed Nu-Jazz tempos while the reactor slowly bled out into the night. Legend holds that Elder Kenji struck the final, deafening kakegoe shout during the terminal retro-burn, keeping time for an ensemble of dying horn players whose instruments were soldered to their lungs by cold-weld sealant. Etched across the titanium bulkhead behind the drum was the final sacred message left for the unborn landing scouts: "Our hands broke against the hides, but the silence died before we did."
